## 5. TANK DESIGN AND STATS (small tanks, big world)

World units are **meters**. Time in seconds. Tanks are deliberately **small relative to the map** so the battlefield feels large and tactical. All values live in `config.ts`.

| Stat | Value |
|---|---|
| Hull size (visual and collision) | 1.6 m wide x 2.6 m long x 0.8 m high; turret 1.0 m diameter, barrel 1.6 m long (this table is the **Standard** class; Scout and Heavy are in Section 28) |
| Health | 100 HP (host can choose 100 or 150) |
| Forward speed | 7 m/s (accel 18 m/s², brake 28 m/s²) |
| Reverse speed | 4 m/s |
| Hull turn speed | 110 degrees/s standing, 70 degrees/s at full speed (smooth curve) |
| Turret turn speed | 260 degrees/s |
| Turbo | speed x1.5 for 3 s, recharges in 6 s (cannot be used at 0 stamina) |
| Handbrake pivot | hull turn speed x1.8 and speed capped at 40% while held |
| Cannon damage | 30 |
| Cannon reload | 1.1 s (reload ring on the crosshair) |
| Cannon shell | speed 55 m/s, lifetime 2.2 s (range 120 m), radius 0.3 m, ricochets off walls once |
| Respawn | 3 s after death, at a safe spawn point, 2 s spawn shield (blinking, cannot be hurt or fire) |

**Movement feel (shared code `stepTank`)**
- Acceleration and braking are smooth curves, not instant. The hull turns slower when moving fast and faster when slow.
- Ground types: normal grass/sand/concrete, **ice** (low friction: velocity keeps drifting, turning has delayed effect), **mud** (speed x0.6), **speed pad** (x1.4 for 2 s).
- Tanks slide along walls and obstacles (no sticking), and bump each other with a small push, spark effect and thud sound.
- Visual feel: hull pitches back slightly on acceleration and forward on braking (max 3 degrees), rolls slightly on sharp turns (max 4 degrees), tracks scroll with speed, dust trail on dry ground, snow spray on ice, mud splash in mud.
- `stepTank(state, input, dt)` lives in `/shared` and is used identically by the server (truth) and the client (prediction).

