## 11. 3D LOOK AND CAMERA

**Renderer:** WebGL, antialiasing on, ACES tone mapping, sRGB output, pixel ratio capped at 1.5 (2 on High). One directional sun with soft shadows (shadow map 2048 High, 1024 Medium, off Low), hemisphere ambient light, map-colored fog. Sky is a gradient dome with low-poly clouds or distant landmarks per map.
**Materials:** `MeshStandardMaterial`, flat colors, slight roughness, thin darker edge or emissive trims for a stylized toy-like look. Ground has a subtle procedural noise texture.
**Performance:** instancing for repeated props (crates, barrels, trees, containers), merged static geometry per map, pooled bullets and particles, frustum culling, max 4 dynamic lights (muzzle flashes). Quality presets Low / Medium / High; **auto-lower quality** if FPS stays below 40 for 5 s.

**Camera (third-person angled chase):** height about 26 m, distance about 22 m behind, pitch about 55 degrees, FOV 60 (adjustable 50 to 80), follows the tank with smooth lerp (0.1) and leads slightly toward the aim direction. **Mouse wheel zoom** between 18 m and 45 m with easing. Small camera shake on firing, hits and explosions (toggle in Settings). Because tanks are small, name tags and health bars have a **fixed screen size**.

**Spectator mode** after death in Last Tank Standing: follow living players (left/right click to switch), free camera option.

