## 31. RULES AND EDGE CASES (bug prevention: implement every line)

| # | Situation | Required behavior |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Two tanks destroy each other on the same server tick | Both die; both get a kill credited; in Last Tank Standing, if that leaves no survivor the round is a **draw and is replayed** (max 2 replays, then both get the round) |
| 2 | Killer disconnects before the kill is shown | Kill stays credited to the killer's name; kill feed still shows it |
| 3 | A shell hits a tank during its spawn shield | The shell is destroyed, no damage, small shield ripple |
| 4 | Shell hits a missile | Missiles have 10 HP and can be destroyed (cannon does 30), explosion at that spot; cluster and guided missiles have 10 HP as well |
| 5 | Two tanks overlap (spawn, pushing) | Push them apart along the center line, 4 m/s separation; never allow permanent overlap; spawn points are chosen so no tank is within 8 m |
| 6 | Tank touches a Power Box on the same tick as another tank | The tank with the lower server-side distance wins; if equal, the earlier input sequence time wins; only one pickup per box |
| 7 | A dead tank touches a Power Box | No pickup |
| 8 | Tank dies holding a stored weapon or buffs | Stored weapon is lost; all timed buffs cleared; no drops |
| 9 | Flag carrier dies, disconnects or leaves | The flag drops at that position; it returns to base after 15 s or when touched by its own team |
| 10 | Your flag is stolen and you carry the enemy flag to your base | No score; the "Your flag is taken!" message shows; you must recover your flag first |
| 11 | Time runs out while a flag is carried | The carrier's team gets no point for it |
| 12 | King of the Hill: dead tanks, tanks inside an EMP | Dead tanks do not count; EMP tanks count normally; contested (two teams or two FFA players) = no points |
| 13 | Safe zone | Final radius 20 m; outside the ring damage is 5 HP per second (not blocked by shield); the ring shrinks linearly from 30 s to 70% of the match time |
| 14 | Mine on a teammate (team modes) | No damage to teammates; in FFA mines hurt everyone including the owner |
| 15 | Airstrike or barrel on the owner | Hurts the owner in FFA, not in team modes; barrel explosions always hurt everyone |
| 16 | Guided missile owner dies or disconnects | The missile detonates at once; the camera returns |
| 17 | Player joins a match in progress | FFA / TDM / CTF / KOTH: joins immediately as a new tank with 0 score and a 3 s spawn (late-join allowed until the last 60 s); Last Tank Standing: spectator until the next round; always allowed up to the room limit |
| 18 | Fewer than 2 tanks left in a running match with no bots (everyone left) | The match ends immediately and shows results; the room goes back to the lobby |
| 19 | Host leaves | Host migrates to the earliest-joined remaining human, everyone gets a toast "[name] is now the host"; the running match continues; the lobby settings stay |
| 20 | Player disconnects | Tank is parked, invulnerable and shown as "Reconnecting..." for 60 s, then removed; the score is kept for the results screen as "left" |
| 21 | Duplicate nickname | Add a suffix: "Sam", "Sam (2)", "Sam (3)" |
| 22 | Nickname invalid (empty, only spaces, HTML) | Replace with "Player" + random 3 digits |
| 23 | Browser tab hidden or minimized | The client sends neutral inputs; after 10 s the player is marked AFK (tank stops, tag shows "AFK"); after 60 s they are removed from the match; they can rejoin |
| 24 | Window resize, fullscreen toggle | The renderer and UI scale instantly; no game state is lost; the aim pin stays correct |
| 25 | Mouse leaves the window | The last aim point is kept; clicks outside are ignored; no stuck fire (fire is cleared when the window loses focus) |
| 26 | Keys stuck after Alt-Tab | Clear all pressed keys and mouse buttons on blur and on visibility change |
| 27 | Clock differences between PCs | The server sends its time; the client keeps an offset and uses server time for all timers shown (match timer, respawn, box timers) |
| 28 | Lag spike | Interpolation extrapolates at most 200 ms; after that the tank is shown frozen with a small "lag" icon; on recovery positions blend within 150 ms |
| 29 | Rematch | Scores, kills and states reset; players keep class, color, and settings; players who left are removed; a player who joined sees the lobby; the host can change settings first |
| 30 | Kick | Kicked player sees "You were removed by the host" and returns to the menu; cannot rejoin the same room for 60 s |
| 31 | Full room | New players see "Room is full" with a "Join as spectator" button (spectators do not count toward the limit, max 6) |
| 32 | Wrong room state | Joining during COUNTDOWN is allowed (they get a tank at the next spawn); joining during RESULTS places them in the lobby |
| 33 | Ties at time up | Sudden death as in Section 9; if no kill/score happens in 60 s the match is a draw and all tied players share first place |
| 34 | Scoreboard order | Kills (high first), then deaths (low first), then damage dealt (high first), then name |
| 35 | Respawn on the same spot repeatedly | The server never uses the same spawn point twice in a row for one player and prefers the point farthest from enemies |
| 36 | Bullets leaving the map | All projectiles are removed at the perimeter wall (ricochet once for shells, other weapons explode); no projectile exists longer than its lifetime |
| 37 | Floating point drift | Positions are rounded to 3 decimals in the shared step function; use fixed dt (1/30 s); never use Date.now() inside the simulation step |
| 38 | Missing assets or models | Always fall back to the code-drawn version; the game must never show a blank screen |
| 39 | Server error | The server logs the error and continues; one room crashing must never crash the others (each room runs in a try/catch loop) |
| 40 | Reconnect to an ended room | Show "That room no longer exists" and return to the menu |

