## 32. SERVER TICK ORDER AND VALIDATION LIMITS

**Order of operations for each server tick (30 Hz).** Keep exactly this order so results are deterministic:
1. Read the newest unprocessed input of each player (use the last input if none arrived; if none for 0.3 s use neutral input).
2. Validate and clamp inputs (see limits below).
3. Update timed effects and cooldowns (buffs, reload, turbo, dash, EMP, spawn shield).
4. Move tanks (`stepTank`), resolve tank-vs-world and tank-vs-tank collisions.
5. Handle fire / weapon use requests (reload and ammo checks), create projectiles.
6. Move projectiles with swept collision; apply hits, ricochets and explosions; apply damage in a consistent order (by projectile creation time).
7. Process pickups (Power Boxes, flags).
8. Process deaths (destruction events, kills, assists, streaks), start respawn timers.
9. Process mode logic (scores, flags, hill zone, safe zone, round and match end).
10. Process respawns and box respawns.
11. Every 3rd tick (about 10 Hz) or per the 20 Hz schedule: build and send snapshots; send queued events immediately.

**Validation limits (server enforces):**
| Item | Limit |
|---|---|
| Move input | forward and turn in [-1, 1] |
| Aim | aim point inside the map bounds; turret turn speed limited to the class value |
| Fire | not faster than the class reload (and 0.9 s minimum for Rapid Fire logic) |
| Weapon use | only if the slot is filled and the weapon is ready |
| Nickname | 1 to 14 characters after trim, no `<` `>` characters |
| Chat message | max 80 characters, max 1 per second, quick-chat only for the first 5 s of a match |
| Room code | 4 characters from the allowed set |
| Messages | max 120 per second per socket; at 200 per second, close the socket |
| Max packet size | 4 KB for client messages |
| Player counts | 2 to 10 humans, 12 tanks total, 6 spectators |
| Speeds | positions that exceed class speed x 1.2 per tick are corrected back by the server |

**Config rule:** every number in Sections 5, 7, 8, 9, 28 and 31 lives in `/shared/config.ts`. A debug command `?debug=1` shows an overlay with: ping, tick rate, snapshot rate, prediction error, entities count, FPS, and lets you change speeds live in Practice mode.

